    <description>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EApplicants must carry out a site appraisal that identifies and analyses the physical and\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eenvironmental characteristics of the site.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe site appraisal must:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Ebe unbiased, balanced and based on factual information\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Ebe structured to align with the stages of the design process, prioritising the key considerations needed to create a well-designed place for both people and nature\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Edemonstrate an understanding of the site within its local and wider context, taking into account both opportunities and constraints\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Edemonstrate a clear assessment of the topics set out in \u2018List 1 site appraisal\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAssessment\u2019, relevant to the scale of the proposed development\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EException:\u003C/strong\u003E Minor developments need only to assess the indicated fields (\u003Cstrong\u003Emust \u003C/strong\u003Eassess), with further considerations referenced in G1.1 which are highlighted as guidance (\u003Cstrong\u003Eshould \u003C/strong\u003Econsider).\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </description>
    <developmentScales>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  "Major Employment Applications",
  "Major Residential Applications (10\u002B homes)",
